# spec_id: eravos.wub-filter · version 1.0.0 · status built · template eravos.tool/1 (STD.fx)
identity:
  id: eravos.wub-filter ; label: Wub Filter ; domain: music ; category: wubs (shown as Wubs)
  purpose: the mouth of a wobble — a filter whose opening is one number, "wub": 0 = closed, 1 = open.
ports:
  in:  in (audio) · mod.wub (±1 passes straight through: the opening — wire Wub Rate here) ·
       mod.cutoff (±1 → ±4800 c) · mod.res (±1 → ±10 Q) · mod.mix (STD.fx)
  out: out (audio)
params: mode [lowpass, bandpass, notch, vowel, comb] · slope [12, 24] · cutoff 30..4000 Hz (closed) · range 0..8 oct ·
  res · position 0..1 · invert · drive · vowelA / vowelB [OO, OH, AH, AE, EH, EE, YOI] · formant ±12 st ·
  comb −1..1 · STD.fx (mix, inGain, outGain, bypass)
behaviour:
  - opening = position + wub (invert: position + 1 − wub) — one audio-rate signal drives every mode
  - lowpass / bandpass / notch: two biquads (24 dB staggered Q; 12 dB = the first only); opening × range × 1200 c on
    .detune, so the mouth opens in octaves from Closed at
  - vowel: three bandpass formants glide from vowelA (closed) to vowelB (open), frequency and band gain, × formant shift
  - comb: feed-forward y = x + comb · x(t − d); d = 1/cutoff closed → 1/(cutoff · 2^range) open (no feedback loop, so
    no 128-sample minimum delay); + comb = peaks, − = hollow notches
  - drive: tanh before the filter, so resonance growls; DC blocked after; each mode carries its own make-up gain
  - no clock of its own: with nothing wired and position 0 it is simply a closed filter
packs: ships [factory] — 11 presets: Classic LP Wub · Yoi Vowel (OO → AH) · Talking Yoi (OH → EE) · Yoi Yoi (OO → YOI) ·
  Riddim Notch · Robot Comb · Hollow Comb (−) · Bandpass Yap · Gentle 12 dB · Screech Reso · Inverted Mouth
acceptance (wub-filter.test.js): the tool contract · position 1 lets more highs through than position 0 · invert
  flips that · Wub Rate wired into wub makes the high band rise and fall at the step's rate · every mode passes sound

